15 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows schematic gene clusters and a metabolic pathway diagram for the biosynthesis and transport of tryptophan in bacteria, indicating genes, intermediates, and transporters. Panels B to D display line graphs measuringbacterial growth \(OD600\), glucose, acetate, tryptophan, serine, and indoleconcentrations in culture supernatants over time under four conditions: CDM-2, CDM-2 plus tryptophan, CDM-2 plus serine, and CDM-2 plus both amino acids. Panel E presents a bar graph quantifying intracellular pmol tryptophan among conditions, indicating in all cases statistically significant differences.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows two MA plots with gene expression log fold changes versus normalized counts for Trp \(left\) and Ser \(right\) conditions, highlighting differentially expressed genes; Panel B displays volcano plots for Trp and Ser with significant genes outlined in Ser; Panel C presents a schematic of the sdaC-sdaA-mtr gene region with overlaid RNA sequencing read coverage across conditions; Panel D includes two bar graphs quantifying sdaA and mtr gene expression under different Trp and Ser conditions; Panel E consists of gene construct diagrams for pSGMC and pGMC, along with a gel electrophoresis image showing DNA and RNA samples confirming amplification; Panel F contains two bar graphs measuring GFP and mCherry fluorescence under various constructs and amino acid treatments.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Scientific figure composed of seven panels labeled A to G, each displaying various bar graphs, scatter plots, or line charts that compare experimental\ngroups. The plots present data such as tryptophan concentration, bacterial load, gene expression levels, and growth curves with statistical significance indicated by asterisks. Groups tested include wild-type, knockout mutants, and various treatments with Trp-depleted diet or administration of the AhR ligand FICZ, highlighting differences in immune response markers and bacterial fitness. Error bars represent variability and axes are labeled with units and gene or condition names.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
